pageType: content
notes: |
  Balance of plant (BOP) and divertor engineering slide. Evaluates the thermal challenge of handling 10 to 20 MW/m² heat flux on divertor strike plates—comparable to rocket exhaust nozzles. Compares power conversion thermodynamic cycles: conventional steam Rankine (33–38% efficiency), supercritical CO2 Brayton (>45% efficiency), and pulsed FRC direct inductive extraction. Details parasitic recirculating electrical loads (cryogenics, heating, pumping) that demand high plasma Q.
elements:
  # Header Kicker
  - elementId: kicker
    elementType: text
    bounds: [50, 26, 600, 16]
    content:
      style: "$kicker"
      text: "05 · SUPPLY-CHAIN BOTTLENECKS"

  # Header Title
  - elementId: title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [50, 42, 860, 30]
    content:
      style: "$title"
      text: "Divertor Heat Flux Rivals Rocket Nozzles; Thermal Conversion Dictates Net Grid Efficiency"

  # Header Subtitle
  - elementId: subtitle
    elementType: text
    bounds: [50, 72, 860, 16]
    content:
      style: "$subtitle"
      text: "Thermal exhaust dissipation (10–20 MW/m²), Brayton vs Rankine balance-of-plant cycles, and recirculating load fractions"

  # Header Divider
  - elementId: header-line
    elementType: line
    bounds: [50, 92, 860, 1]
    points: "0,0 860,0"
    border: {style: solid, width: 0.8, color: "$border"}

  # Panel 1: Divertor
  - elementId: p1-bg
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [50, 106, 276, 268]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$cardBg"}
    border: {style: solid, width: 0.8, color: "$border"}

  - elementId: p1-header
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [50, 106, 276, 28]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$titleNavy"}

  - elementId: p1-title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [58, 111, 260, 18]
    content:
      fontSize: 9
      bold: true
      color: "$white"
      text: "1. DIVERTOR HEAT EXHAUST"

  - elementId: p1-content
    elementType: text
    bounds: [58, 142, 260, 216]
    content:
      fontSize: 8.3
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.35
      text: |
        <p><b>Extreme Surface Heat Flux:</b></p>
        <p>Core exhaust power streams along the scrape-off layer (SOL) onto narrow divertor strike plates, generating peak continuous heat fluxes of <b>10–20 MW/m²</b> (comparable to spacecraft atmospheric re-entry).</p>
        <p><br><b>Engineering Solutions:</b></p>
        <p>• <b>Detached Divertor Regimes:</b> Noble gas puffing (Argon/Neon) radiates exhaust energy uniformly before striking solid armor.</p>
        <p>• <b>Advanced Magnetic Topologies:</b> Super-X long-legged divertors (MAST-U) expand strike surface area 10-fold.</p>
        <p>• <b>Liquid Metal Walls:</b> Flowing liquid Lithium / PbLi films eliminate solid surface erosion and crack formation.</p>

  # Panel 2: Power Conversion
  - elementId: p2-bg
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [342, 106, 276, 268]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$cardBg"}
    border: {style: solid, width: 0.8, color: "$border"}

  - elementId: p2-header
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [342, 106, 276, 28]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$accentBlue"}

  - elementId: p2-title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [350, 111, 260, 18]
    content:
      fontSize: 9
      bold: true
      color: "$white"
      text: "2. POWER CONVERSION CYCLES"

  - elementId: p2-content
    elementType: text
    bounds: [350, 142, 260, 216]
    content:
      fontSize: 8.3
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.35
      text: |
        <p><b>Steam Rankine Cycle (Baseline):</b></p>
        <p>Conventional utility standard; thermal efficiency ~33–38% at 350–450°C. Requires massive cooling water infrastructure and large civil footprint.</p>
        <p><br><b>Supercritical CO₂ (sCO₂) Brayton:</b></p>
        <p>High-temperature cycle (&gt;550°C); delivers <b>&gt;45% net thermal efficiency</b>. Turbomachinery is 10× more compact than steam, significantly lowering plant capital costs.</p>
        <p><br><b>Direct Inductive Recovery (FRC):</b></p>
        <p>Employed by Helion; magnetic fields compress and re-expand plasmoids, inducing current directly into external pickup coils at <b>&gt;85% theoretical efficiency</b>, eliminating steam turbine islands entirely.</p>

  # Panel 3: Recirculating Load
  - elementId: p3-bg
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [634, 106, 276, 268]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$cardBg"}
    border: {style: solid, width: 0.8, color: "$border"}

  - elementId: p3-header
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [634, 106, 276, 28]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$orangeAccent"}

  - elementId: p3-title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [642, 111, 260, 18]
    content:
      fontSize: 9
      bold: true
      color: "$white"
      text: "3. PARASITIC RECIRCULATING LOAD"

  - elementId: p3-content
    elementType: text
    bounds: [642, 142, 260, 216]
    content:
      fontSize: 8.3
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.35
      text: |
        <p><b>Internal Parasitic Electrical Demand:</b></p>
        <p>A fusion plant consumes substantial internal electricity before delivering net power to the transmission grid:</p>
        <p>• Cryogenic refrigeration (20K HTS / 4K LTS)</p>
        <p>• RF Heating &amp; Current Drive (ECRH, ICRF)</p>
        <p>• Primary coolant &amp; liquid metal circulation pumps</p>
        <p>• Tritium recovery &amp; isotope separation plant</p>
        <p><br><b>Net Plant Gain Threshold:</b></p>
        <p>Parasitic loads typically represent <b>15–30% of gross generation</b>. If scientific gain falls below \( Q_{\mathrm{plasma}} \approx 15 \), the entire electrical output is consumed internally, resulting in zero net grid power.</p>

  # Watch Indicators Band
  - elementId: watch-bg
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [50, 384, 860, 74]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$cardBg"}
    border: {style: solid, width: 0.8, color: "$border"}

  - elementId: watch-accent
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [50, 384, 4, 74]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$orangeAccent"}

  - elementId: watch-label
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 398, 118, 46]
    content:
      fontSize: 7.5
      bold: true
      color: "$titleNavy"
      lineHeight: 1.3
      text: |
        <p>WATCH INDICATORS</p>
        <p>2026–2030</p>

  - elementId: watch-1
    elementType: text
    bounds: [190, 398, 250, 46]
    content:
      fontSize: 7.5
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.3
      text: |
        <p><b>Peak divertor heat flux (MW/m²)</b></p>
        <p>10–20 MW/m² continuous; detached regimes are the mitigation path</p>

  - elementId: watch-2
    elementType: text
    bounds: [450, 398, 240, 46]
    content:
      fontSize: 7.5
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.3
      text: |
        <p><b>Net thermal efficiency (%)</b></p>
        <p>33–38% steam Rankine; &gt;45% claimed for sCO₂ Brayton</p>

  - elementId: watch-3
    elementType: text
    bounds: [700, 398, 210, 46]
    content:
      fontSize: 7.5
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.3
      text: |
        <p><b>Recirculating load share</b></p>
        <p>Above ~30% of gross output, net plant gain collapses</p>

  # Bottom Synthesis Strip
  - elementId: synth-bg
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [50, 472, 860, 32]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$panelBg"}
    border: {style: solid, width: 0.8, color: "$border"}

  - elementId: synth-accent
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [50, 472, 4, 32]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$accentBlue"}

  - elementId: synth-text
    elementType: text
    bounds: [62, 478, 836, 20]
    content:
      fontSize: 8.5
      color: "$ink"
      text: "<b>Engineering Takeaway:</b> Plant balance of plant constitutes &gt;40% of total capital expenditure; advanced sCO2 cycles and detached divertor regimes are critical to grid profitability."

  # Footer Line
  - elementId: footer-line
    elementType: line
    bounds: [50, 514, 860, 1]
    points: "0,0 860,0"
    border: {style: solid, width: 0.6, color: "$border"}

  # Footer Source Left
  - elementId: footer-source
